f the positive and negative whole numbers, and zero: $…,-3,\\,-2,\\,-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2,\\,3,…$\n\n- The rationals consist of all numbers that can be written as the ratio of two integers.\n\nNow, let's go through each number in turn.\n\n- $\\frac{1}{10}$ is not a natural number.\n\n- $\\frac{1}{10}$ is not an integer.\n\n- $\\frac{1}{10}$ is a rational number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is, \"III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "44dc1f4c-fd4e-52ad-a63a-2ecc1e1041de" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433613}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433612 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433610 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e712e82-fa0f-5c35-8341-987cad89094f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433584} {:answer/id #uuid "5a5526aa-d152-5495-bbcb-6f1e1ee497c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433591} {:answer/id #uuid "96e7edb9-c054-584a-a80a-d979fedb4496" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433597} {:answer/id #uuid "99522998-d655-5aee-9ba1-5f3e13bc3006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433598} {:answer/id #uuid "b0b741c4-7edd-5fb2-9681-7f1843d11f19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433599}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433598} :answer-field/id #uuid "189f8c27-4698-52fa-b757-7d2b24c8aa2a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433603}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "eb2e9e07-c134-569e-a208-041621377fa3" :question/math-academy-id "q-99311" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are integers?\n\nI. $100$\n\nII. $-5$\n\nIII. $-\\frac{9}{2}$" :question/worked-solution "The integers consist of all positive and negative whole numbers and zero.\n\n$$\n…,-3,\\,-2,\\,-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2,\\,3,…\n$$\n\n \n\nOf the given numbers, $100$ and $-5$ are integers, but $-\\frac{9}{2}$ is not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} :step/id #uuid "63f2e9a0-ccd8-53e1-823a-f93d8c2355e1"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433613 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433608 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ef60037-3b80-5502-933c-09d72a5ba319" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433585} {:answer/id #uuid "20049e96-ae01-5c45-9a3c-1f7838319008" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433586} {:answer/id #uuid "32cb23a7-2f0e-5f7f-aacf-0afbcb6147d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433587} {:answer/id #uuid "52d54b01-b14b-5e76-b8dd-55960b680252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433589} {:answer/id #uuid "d85a86a3-e5b3-5d88-8a74-b8f032a1e5b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433601}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433601} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cd1f0fa-8af8-54fb-b456-0eee7ce3fb92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433605}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "46c072ed-28fe-5e0e-96d0-a316d330f872" :question/math-academy-id "q-93611" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $-10$ is a natural number\n\nII. $-10$ is an integer\n\nIII. $-10$ is a rational number" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall our definitions.\n\n- The natural numbers consist of all positive whole numbers: $1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,4,\\,5,…$\n\n- The integers consist of all of the positive and negative whole numbers, and zero: $…,-3,\\,-2,\\,-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2,\\,3,…$\n\n- The rationals consist of all numbers that can be written as the ratio of two integers.\n\nNow, let's go through each number in turn.\n\n- $-10$ is not a natural number.\n\n- $-10$ is an integer.\n\n- $-10$ is a rational number because it can be written as $\\frac{(-10)}{1}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is, \"II and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "678e552d-7057-5896-a457-bfa4af875ece" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433615}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433614 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152878 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d28a50a6-7308-5e7d-9506-1e4175511186" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151776} {:answer/id #uuid "ed8b1e51-4f39-5465-8987-f4a307226cf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151777} {:answer/id #uuid "171962fe-cdfc-56f5-897b-aa03946cf77e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151778} {:answer/id #uuid "61310617-8554-57e3-9ce9-7002b33a7a58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151779} {:answer/id #uuid "643cedf7-507f-5e63-91cf-0aa5f8a535ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151780}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151780} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd4be8de-607c-5578-91b6-081cf9216fab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151775}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c0d528fe-7741-52a6-a947-e2ff7f9a758d" :question/math-academy-id "q-98382" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $-2$ is a natural number\n\nII. $-2$ is an integer\n\nIII. $-2$ is a rational number" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall our definitions.\n\n- The natural numbers consist of all positive whole numbers: $1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,4,\\,5,…$\n\n- The integers consist of all of the positive and negative whole numbers, and zero: $…,-3,\\,-2,\\,-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2,\\,3,…$\n\n- The rationals consist of any number that can be written as the ratio of two integers.\n\nNow, let's go through each number in turn.\n\n- $-2$ is not a natural number.\n\n- $-2$ is an integer.\n\n- $-2$ is a rational number because it can be written as $\\frac{(-2)}{1}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is, \"II and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "9656a63a-73b0-53ca-9b94-ede50eec4768" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433612}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433615 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433609 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57a6471b-bd77-5aee-aeff-e9d5f4387baf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433590} {:answer/id #uuid "66d9b2ee-4fe7-59c8-9132-d913e4e61062" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433592} {:answer/id #uuid "75c7099d-8ae5-5ce9-8677-484e3279c83b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433594} {:answer/id #uuid "77a50393-7099-5a74-b6fa-5abc6300ec01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433595} {:answer/id #uuid "b3c8f7ea-0cb0-5b68-9325-dd9c3a2362cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433600}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433595} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e18ef21-c07b-584b-a353-bc2e107acf2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433604}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "de7db80c-f818-55cb-b186-c1d21190ea48" :question/math-academy-i